WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.218 --> 00:00:01.434
♪ (intro music) ♪

00:00:05.499 --> 00:00:06.507
Give me one minute

00:00:06.507 --> 00:00:09.242
and I'll show you how Cloud Logging
can help you better understand

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.506
your infrastructure and apps

00:00:10.506 --> 00:00:12.923
by aggregating and visualizing log data.

00:00:13.435 --> 00:00:16.947
Cloud Logging collects log data
from Google Cloud services automatically,

00:00:16.947 --> 00:00:18.898
or any custom log source

00:00:18.898 --> 00:00:22.708
through Cloud Logging agents,
APIs, and client libraries,

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:26.753
and gives you complete control to decide
how and where to store the logs.

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:28.551
Once the logs are in Cloud Logging,

00:00:28.551 --> 00:00:29.899
the Log Router funnels them

00:00:29.899 --> 00:00:32.346
to Cloud Storage or BigQuery
for analytics,

00:00:32.346 --> 00:00:37.207
or streams the logs via Cloud Pub/Sub
to custom third-party destinations.

00:00:37.585 --> 00:00:40.162
Log Explorer gives you
powerful capabilities

00:00:40.162 --> 00:00:41.999
to find the logs you're searching for.

00:00:42.364 --> 00:00:45.926
You can also use Cloud Logging
to convert logs to log-based metrics

00:00:45.926 --> 00:00:48.794
for monitoring, alerting,
analyzing, and visualizing.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.099
Your error logs sent to Cloud Logging

00:00:51.099 --> 00:00:53.404
are automatically analyzed
by Error Reporting

00:00:53.404 --> 00:00:56.588
to give you a centralized
error management interface

00:00:56.588 --> 00:00:59.984
that counts and aggregates
application crashes and errors.

00:01:00.399 --> 00:01:01.880
From a security perspective,

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:05.104
all your data is encrypted
at rest and in transit.

00:01:05.461 --> 00:01:08.330
All your security focused
immutable Audit Logs

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:11.253
are automatically available
in Cloud Logging,

00:01:11.253 --> 00:01:14.134
telling you who did what, where, and when.

00:01:14.516 --> 00:01:16.293
And with Access Transparency logs,

00:01:16.293 --> 00:01:17.966
you can always stay in compliance,

00:01:17.966 --> 00:01:21.258
because it captures the actions
Google personnel takes

00:01:21.258 --> 00:01:22.639
while offering you support.

00:01:22.872 --> 00:01:25.952
You can use the Cloud Console APIs
to use Cloud Logging.

00:01:26.176 --> 00:01:28.421
It comes with a very generous free tier

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.335
to make it easy for you to get started,

00:01:30.335 --> 00:01:32.254
and affordable pricing thereafter.

00:01:32.584 --> 00:01:35.390
So next time you're looking
to use logs for troubleshooting,

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:37.248
take a minute to look at Cloud Logging.

00:01:37.248 --> 00:01:40.945
To learn more, check out
<i>cloud.google.com/logging</i>

